    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d725">

                <pb facs="0813" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.51/899: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-07T17:00:00-05:00">April 7, 1933—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Your 30, April 4, 7 p.m., and your despatches 2001 and 2007.<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d725-f1"/> Do you believe that the proposed allotment of 33% of all
                    available exchange to Great Britain represents a fair proportion for that
                    country taking into consideration (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Argentina’s
                    purchases of British goods, (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) remittances to
                    Great Britain of income from investments, et cetera, and (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) frozen credits?</p>
                <p>Would the 33 percent include the service of the proposed loan of 10,000,000
                    pounds?</p>
                <p>What percentage of exchange should be allotted to the United States if placed on
                    a similar basis?</p>
                <p>If this allotment is granted to the British do you consider it advisable to ask
                    for an allotment for the United States, as set forth in the preceding
                    paragraph?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d725-f1" n="94" xml:id="d725-f1-content">
